VERDICT: REJECTED
The diff does not satisfy core M0 runtime requirements; it introduces useful scaffolding but misses multiple blocking deliverables from the milestone definition.

Critical findings:
- Scheduler architecture is not BullMQ/Redis. `packages/runtime/src/scheduler.ts` implements an in-memory queue (`InMemoryScheduler`), and there is no implemented `@agent-os/scheduler` package with BullMQ queues (`executions`, `delayed`, `approvals`, `replay`, `cleanup`). This is a direct miss against the central M0 requirement.
- Required monorepo restructure was not performed. Workspace remains `packages/*` and `apps/*` (`pnpm-workspace.yaml`), not `packages/agent-os/packages/*` and `packages/agent-os/apps/*`.
- Runtime commit/recovery semantics are incomplete. Worker events/checkpoints are written, but the required four-phase step commit (event -> checkpoint -> agent_state commit -> BullMQ ACK) is not implemented end-to-end; no BullMQ ACK exists; `agent_state` is not committed per step boundary in runtime flow.
